cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Philadelphia Gap: data appendix"
message: "If you use these data or figures, please cite this appendix and the underlying FARS and PennDOT sources."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Quistberg
    given-names: D. Alex
    email: daq26@drexel.edu
    affiliation: "Urban Health Collaborative, Drexel University Dornsife School of Public Health"
abstract: >-
  Interactive data appendix accompanying an article in The Conversation on
  Philadelphia's traffic fatality rate relative to New York, Chicago,
  Washington and Boston. Covers city-year death rates 2010-2024, a ranking of
  the 40 largest US cities, victim modes, crash-circumstance flags compared
  across 2015-2019 and 2020-2024, two Philadelphia corridors, a neighborhood
  map, census-tract income quartiles, and Philadelphia deaths 1975-2025.
keywords:
  - traffic safety
  - road traffic injury
  - pedestrian safety
  - Philadelphia
  - FARS
  - health equity
  - Vision Zero
